---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout title="Privacy Policy">
    <main class="container mx-auto px-4 py-8 max-w-4xl">
        <!-- Header Section -->
        <header class="mb-12">
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Privacy Policy for {{name}} serving {{location}}</h1>
            <div class="flex items-center text-gray-600">
                <span class="font-medium">Last updated:</span>
                <span class="ml-2">{{policy_date}}</span>
            </div>
        </header>

        <!-- Introduction -->
        <section class="mb-10">
            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
                This Privacy Notice explains how <span class="font-semibold">{{name}}</span> ("us") handles and protects personal data when you use our website or request our locksmith services in <span class="font-semibold">{{location}}</span> including emergency call-outs, lock repairs and security work.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mt-4">
                We keep things straightforward: we only use information that we need to act promptly, confirm you are entitled to request access or lock work, complete the job safely, and meet our legal and operational responsibilities.
            </p>
        </section>

        <div class="border-t border-gray-300 my-10"></div>

        <!-- About Us -->
        <section class="mb-10">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">About us and when this policy applies</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">
                {{name}} is a local locksmith business covering <span class="font-semibold">{{location}}</span> and nearby districts. This notice applies when you:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4">
                <li>use our website;</li>
                <li>ask for pricing or arrange an appointment (especially out-of-hours emergencies);</li>
                <li>communicate with us (e.g., web form or in person);</li>
                <li>provide feedback.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                We handle personal data under the UK General Data Protection Regulation and the Data Protection Act 2018.
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- What Information We Collect -->
        <section class="mb-10">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">What information we collect</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">
                The specific data we collect depends on the type of work you request (emergency entry is different to a booked lock change).
            </p>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded-lg mb-6">
                <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Data you give us</h3>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
                    <li><span class="font-medium">Contact details:</span> your name and contact details (such as email).</li>
                    <li><span class="font-medium">Address and location:</span> the service address and helpful directions (to help us find you quickly).</li>
                    <li><span class="font-medium">Service request details:</span> what's happened (e.g., locked out, a snapped key, a jammed or broken lock, break-in damage) and when it occurred.</li>
                    <li><span class="font-medium">Lock and door details:</span> door type (such as uPVC), lock type (for example, a euro cylinder or multipoint system), and the outcome you need.</li>
                    <li><span class="font-medium">Photos/videos you provide:</span> images of the lock face, door alignment, or damage to help us understand what's needed (including whether minimal-damage entry is likely).</li>
                    <li><span class="font-medium">Access verification information (where appropriate):</span> information to confirm you are authorised to request entry or lock changes (see "Access verification").</li>
                    <li><span class="font-medium">Billing details:</span> invoices, payment references, and records (we don't keep full card numbers if you pay via a secure provider).</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded-lg mb-6">
                <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Data collected via our website</h3>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
                    <li><span class="font-medium">Usage information:</span> IP address, browser type, pages viewed, and basic logs used for security and performance.</li>
                    <li><span class="font-medium">Cookies:</span> see the "Cookies" section below.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded-lg">
                <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Sensitive information</h3>
                <p>
                    We don't usually require special category data (e.g., health information). If you voluntarily provide it in an emergency (for example, additional support needs), we use it only to support your request and keep it to a minimum.
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- How We Use Information -->
        <section class="mb-10">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">How we use your information and the legal reasons for doing so</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">
                We use your data to deliver services, keep records, and run our business. Where relevant, we rely on lawful bases such as performance of a contract, compliance with legal duties, and legitimate interests (balanced against your rights).
            </p>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded-lg">
                <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">What we do with your information</h3>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
                    <li><span class="font-medium">Handling enquiries and appointments:</span> confirming details, providing ETA updates, and completing work (e.g., emergency entry, lock repairs, lock changes, securing after a break-in).</li>
                    <li><span class="font-medium">Providing quotes and suitable options:</span> discussing lock types (e.g., cylinders, upgrades, and multipoint systems) and what's suitable for your door and security needs.</li>
                    <li><span class="font-medium">Confirming entitlement and preventing misuse:</span> ensuring we only assist where there is a lawful right to access the property.</li>
                    <li><span class="font-medium">Aftercare and service quality:</span> dealing with questions, issues, and guarantee support where offered.</li>
                    <li><span class="font-medium">Operational requirements:</span> accounting, tax records, insurance administration, and keeping appropriate job records for health and safety and dispute resolution.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Access Verification -->
        <section class="mb-10">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Access verification for entry and lock work in {{location}}</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">
                Because locksmith work can involve access to premises and security changes, we may need to confirm you are entitled to request the work. This is particularly relevant for lockouts, lost keys, and burglary-related work.
            </p>
            <p class="mb-4">
                Depending on the situation, we may ask for appropriate confirmation such as:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4">
                <li>photo ID showing your name; and/or</li>
                <li>evidence linking you to the address (e.g., a tenancy document or recent bill, or confirmation from a landlord/agent); and/or</li>
                <li>confirmation from a relevant party (for example, a landlord, letting agent, or facilities manager for commercial premises).</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                We keep this proportionate, often noting that checks were completed rather than retaining full copies.
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Data Sharing -->
        <section class="mb-10">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Sharing your information</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">
                We never sell your information. We may share it where necessary to provide services or meet legal obligations, for example with:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4">
                <li>payment and invoicing services;</li>
                <li>lock and parts suppliers (e.g., sourcing cylinders or multipoint mechanisms);</li>
                <li>website hosting and IT providers;</li>
                <li>insurers and professional advisers (for claims or advice);</li>
                <li>subcontractors (only where needed to deliver the service, with appropriate controls).</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                We share only what is necessary for the specific purpose.
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- International Transfers -->
        <section class="mb-10">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">International transfers</h2>
            <p>
                Some providers (such as cloud hosting or email platforms) may process data outside the UK. Where a restricted transfer applies, we use appropriate safeguards (for example, international transfer safeguards or equivalent arrangements).
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Data Retention -->
        <section class="mb-10">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Data retention</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">
                We keep personal data only for as long as needed for the purposes described above, including legal and accounting requirements.
            </p>
            <p class="mb-4">
                By way of example:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
                <li><span class="font-medium">Invoices and job records:</span> often retained for up to six years to meet tax and accounting requirements.</li>
                <li><span class="font-medium">Guarantee/warranty support:</span> retained for the duration of any warranty plus a reasonable period for administration and dispute resolution.</li>
                <li><span class="font-medium">Verification notes:</span> kept only as long as needed to demonstrate responsible practice and address disputes, then minimised or deleted.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- Data Security -->
        <section class="mb-10">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Keeping your data safe</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">
                We use reasonable security measures appropriate to a mobile service business, such as:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4">
                <li>access controls on devices and accounts;</li>
                <li>secure storage of digital records;</li>
                <li>limiting access to customer details;</li>
                <li>secure deletion when information is no longer needed.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                No system is 100% secure, but we work to reduce risk and respond appropriately to suspected incidents.
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Your Rights -->
        <section class="mb-10">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Your rights</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">
                You have rights over your personal data, including the right to:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4">
                <li>access your data;</li>
                <li>correct inaccurate data;</li>
                <li>request erasure (in certain circumstances);</li>
                <li>restrict processing;</li>
                <li>data portability (where applicable);</li>
                <li>object to processing based on legitimate interests; and</li>
                <li>withdraw consent where we rely on consent.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                If you want to exercise a right, we may need to verify your identity and will respond within the required timeframes.
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Marketing -->
        <section class="mb-10">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Marketing preferences</h2>
            <p>
                If you opt in to hear about services (for example, security upgrades), you can opt out at any time. We keep marketing proportionate and relevant.
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Cookies -->
        <section class="mb-10">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Cookies and website analytics</h2>
            <p>
                Our website may use cookies and similar technologies to:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mt-2">
                <li>keep the site working properly (essential cookies);</li>
                <li>analyse how the site is used and improve it (analytics cookies, where used).</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mt-4">
                Where required, we provide controls to accept or reject non-essential cookies.
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Reviews -->
        <section class="mb-10">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Reviews and public feedback</h2>
            <p>
                If you leave a review on a third-party platform, your review is processed under that platform's privacy terms. If we display reviews on our website, we generally show only publicly available information (e.g., name or initial, star rating, and review text where permitted).
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Children's Data -->
        <section class="mb-10">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Children's data</h2>
            <p>
                Our services are generally intended for adults requesting work on a property they occupy or manage. If we become aware we have collected a child's personal data inappropriately, we will take steps to delete it.
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Changes -->
        <section class="mb-10">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Changes to this notice</h2>
            <p>
                We may update this notice from time to time to reflect changes in services, legal requirements, or how we process data. The last updated date at the top shows when it was last updated.
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Contact Info (Optional - You can add this) -->

    </main>
</MainLayout>